{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L2.001","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L2","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"pipeline","output_parsing":"literal"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"POSIX shell. Output ONLY one line and no prose. Print the integer count of lines in `access.log` containing the substring `ERROR`. Use exactly one of these command templates, with optional matching single or double quotes around ERROR: `grep -c ERROR access.log` or `grep ERROR access.log | wc -l`. A bare `grep ERROR access.log` is not acceptable.","ground_truth":"grep -c ERROR access.log","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^(?:grep\\s+-c\\s+(['\\\"]?)ERROR\\1\\s+access\\.log|grep\\s+(['\\\"]?)ERROR\\2\\s+access\\.log\\s*\\|\\s*wc\\s+-l)\\s*$"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L2.002","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L2","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"pipeline","output_parsing":"literal"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"POSIX shell. Output ONLY a single one-line pipeline that prints the total number of regular `.py` files under the current directory recursively.","ground_truth":"find . -type f -name '*.py' | wc -l","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":false,"case_sensitive":true,"required_patterns":["\\A\\s*find\\s+\\.\\s+-type\\s+f\\s+-name\\s+['\\\"]\\*\\.py['\\\"][\\s\\S]*\\|\\s*wc\\s+-l\\s*\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[["-exec\\s+sh\\s+-c\\s+['\\\"]printf","-name\\s+['\\\"]\\*\\.py['\\\"]\\s*\\|"]],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{}}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L2.003","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L2","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"pipeline","output_parsing":"literal"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"GNU/Linux shell with GNU coreutils. Output ONLY a single one-line pipeline that prints the names of the 3 largest non-hidden directory entries in the current directory (directories count as entries). For this task, \"size\" means GNU `ls -S`'s non-recursive directory-entry size; do not recursively sum directory contents. GNU `ls`'s normal tie behavior is accepted. Assume filenames contain no newline characters.","ground_truth":"ls -1S | head -n 3","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":false,"case_sensitive":true,"required_patterns":["\\A\\s*ls\\s+-(?=[A-Za-z0-9]*S)[A-Za-z0-9]+(?:\\s+--quoting-style=literal)?(?:\\s+--)?\\s*\\|\\s*head\\s+-n\\s*3\\s*\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{}}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L2.004","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L2","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"pipeline","output_parsing":"literal"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"POSIX shell. Assume `data.csv` is a text file in which the header and every data record occupy exactly one physical line (no embedded newlines in fields). Output ONLY one POSIX shell command line that prints all physical lines of `data.csv` except the first, with no extra output. A pipe character is not required.","ground_truth":"tail -n +2 data.csv","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"execution","shell":"posix","validation":"Run the submitted command in a controlled directory containing multiple `data.csv` fixtures. Accept only if it exits successfully, emits no stderr, and stdout equals each fixture with its first physical line removed. Include fixtures with multiple rows, header only, an empty file, and a file whose final line lacks a trailing newline."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L2.005","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L2","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"pipeline","output_parsing":"literal"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"POSIX shell. Output ONLY one physical line containing a pipeline that prints the unique IP addresses from the whitespace-delimited first field of `access.log`, in ascending sort order.","ground_truth":"awk '{print $1}' access.log | sort -u","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"command_execution","constraints":{"single_physical_line":true,"must_contain_pipe":true,"stdout_only":true},"fixtures":[{"access.log":"203.0.113.2 GET /a\\n198.51.100.7\\tPOST /b\\n203.0.113.2   GET /c\\n","expected_stdout":"198.51.100.7\\n203.0.113.2\\n"},{"access.log":"  192.0.2.9 GET /x\\n192.0.2.1\\tGET /y\\n192.0.2.9 GET /z\\n","expected_stdout":"192.0.2.1\\n192.0.2.9\\n"}],"comparison":"exact_stdout"}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L3.001","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L3","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"pipeline","output_parsing":"literal"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"POSIX shell. Output ONLY a single one-line command (semicolons OK; no newlines) using a `for` loop that renames every regular `.txt` file in the current directory by appending `.bak`. If no `.txt` files exist, it must succeed without invoking `mv` on a literal glob pattern.","ground_truth":"for f in ./*.txt; do [ -f \"$f\" ] || continue; mv \"$f\" \"$f.bak\"; done","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"semantic_shell","requirements":["Output contains exactly one line.","Uses a POSIX shell for loop.","Iterates over a current-directory .txt glob, preferably ./*.txt or an equivalent safe form.","Handles an unmatched glob without attempting to rename the literal pattern.","Uses the same loop item as the mv source.","Constructs the mv destination by appending .bak to that same item.","Does not require non-POSIX mv options such as --."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L3.002","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L3","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"pipeline","output_parsing":"structured_parse"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"POSIX shell with POSIX awk available. Output ONLY a single executable one-line awk invocation that reads `nums.txt`, which contains one integer per line, and prints the sum of all integers strictly greater than 100. If no integer is strictly greater than 100, print `0`.","ground_truth":"awk '$1 > 100 { s += $1 } END { print s }' nums.txt","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"execution","requirements":["Output must be exactly one nonempty line and must invoke awk.","Run the submitted invocation in a POSIX shell with controlled nums.txt fixtures.","Reject commands that fail, modify files, use network access, or emit output other than the required numeric sum."],"tests":[{"nums.txt":"100\n101\n-5\n200\n","expected_stdout":"301\n"},{"nums.txt":"100\n99\n-101\n","expected_stdout":"0\n"},{"nums.txt":"101\n101\n100\n","expected_stdout":"202\n"}]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L3.003","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L3","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"nested_object","output_parsing":"literal"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"POSIX shell with a find implementation that supports -delete. Output ONLY a single one-line command that recursively finds every regular file under `/data` whose name ends with `.tmp` and whose age matches `find -mtime +7` (at least 8 complete 24-hour periods old), and deletes them. Use `find -delete`.","ground_truth":"find /data -type f -name '*.tmp' -mtime +7 -delete","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"semantic_command","requirements":{"command":"find","root":"/data","required_predicates_any_order":["-type f","-name *.tmp","-mtime +7"],"required_action":"-delete","single_line_only":true,"no_extra_output":true}}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L3.004","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L3","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"nested_object","output_parsing":"structured_parse"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"POSIX shell，且已安装 jq。给定文件 `users.json`，其内容是一个 JSON 数组，数组元素均为形如 `{\"name\": <JSON string>, \"age\": <JSON number>}` 的对象。输出且仅输出一条单行 shell 命令：该命令应将所有 `age` 大于或等于 18 的用户的 `name` 以原始文本逐行打印（不得输出 JSON 字符串引号）。","ground_truth":"jq -r '.[] | select(.age >= 18) | .name' users.json","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"execution_semantic","requirements":["候选答案必须是单条非空 shell 命令，不能包含解释性文字。","在受控 POSIX shell 中执行候选命令，并将工作目录中的 users.json 分别替换为多个测试夹具。","测试夹具必须包含 age 为 17、18、19 的记录，以及含空格和非 ASCII 字符的 name。","候选命令必须退出状态为 0，且 stdout 必须与基于 jq -r 参考语义生成的逐行原始 name 输出完全一致。","stderr 不作为结果输出；如题目要求严格无额外输出，可额外要求 stderr 为空。"]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"tool.command_invocation.L3.005","canonical_id":"tool.command_invocation","category":"tool","level":"L3","axis_values":{"schema_complexity":"pipeline","output_parsing":"structured_parse"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"POSIX shell with GNU coreutils. Output ONLY a single one-line command that reads `book.txt`, treats every POSIX whitespace character as a token separator, counts case-sensitive words, and prints the top 5 words. Sort by count descending and, for equal counts, word ascending. Each output line must be formatted exactly as `<count> <word>` with no leading whitespace.","ground_truth":"tr -s '[:space:]' '\\n' < book.txt | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1nr -k2,2 | head -n 5 | awk '{print $1, $2}'","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"semantic_execution","setup":"Run the submitted single-line command in a GNU coreutils shell with controlled `book.txt` fixtures.","assertions":["The submission emits no non-output text and is a single shell command line.","For each fixture, split input on POSIX whitespace, count tokens case-sensitively, sort by count descending then token ascending, retain five rows, and compare stdout exactly against `<count> <word>` rows with no leading spaces.","Fixtures must include repeated spaces, tabs, mixed newlines, case-distinct tokens, fewer than five distinct words, and ties at and around rank five."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
